1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,320
Dad, school is so far.
It's a ten-minute walk!

2
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:11,740
Ten minutes? When I was
your age...

3
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:15,523
Every morning, I would
wake up before the

4
00:00:15,523 --> 00:00:19,250
rooster, tie my books with
string, and start walking.

5
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:26,301
Not ten minutes. Hours.
Hill after hill, with no

6
00:00:26,301 --> 00:00:27,070
shoes.

7
00:00:27,970 --> 00:00:33,393
Then came the Blue Nile. I
would hold my books over

8
00:00:33,393 --> 00:00:38,391
my head. There was always
a hungry crocodile. I

9
00:00:38,391 --> 00:00:39,880
never stopped.

10
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:43,937
Next, the Chebera
Churchura jungle.

11
00:00:43,937 --> 00:00:48,357
Elephants used to block
the path, so I would walk

12
00:00:48,357 --> 00:00:49,890
right under them.

13
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:54,948
Then I would climb the
Simien mountains. The

14
00:00:54,948 --> 00:00:59,390
geladas just used to watch
me, without helping.

15
00:01:00,290 --> 00:01:05,270
And then, the volcano.
Erta Ale. I would jump

16
00:01:05,270 --> 00:01:11,025
from rock to rock over the
lava. My feet were always

17
00:01:11,025 --> 00:01:11,910
on fire.

18
00:01:12,810 --> 00:01:18,342
Finally, wet and smoking,
I would reach school. And

19
00:01:18,342 --> 00:01:22,030
every day, my teacher
would say...

20
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:24,440
You're late again!
